1	//! TypeScript 7.1 checker backend, on by default (ADR 0026; `--no-checker` turns it off).
2	//!
3	//! Asks TypeScript's checker for the props of each component the structural pass found, and hands
4	//! `caliper-docgen-core` a [`SemanticOutcome`] to merge (ADR 0006, ADR 0007). The checker is the `tsrs` crates, linked
5	//! in and run on threads of their own; it is always compiled in and enabled at run time. Any failure to start or
6	//! finish (a checker thread that cannot be spawned, a timeout) yields an outcome with no components and one
7	//! diagnostic, never an error: the structural result is complete on its own.
8	//!
9	//! This slice answers function components by the exports the extractor recorded for them (a name, `default`, or the
10	//! property of an exported component a sub-component is attached to); a generic one whose first type parameter
11	//! declares a default is read at that default (`instantiate`). Class components, overloaded components and union props
12	//! types keep their structural result and say why.
13	
14	#![deny(missing_docs)]
